[al:新概念英语（四）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Beauty]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.53]Lesson 24 | 第24课
[00:02.18]Beauty | 美
[00:08.00]What do glimpses of beauty, either in nature or art, often suggest to the human mind? | 对美的一瞥，无论是自然美还是艺术美，常常向人的心灵暗示什么？
[00:17.37]A young man sees a sunset and, | 一个年轻人看到日落，
[00:20.00]unable to understand or to express the emotion that it rouses in him, | 由于无法理解或表达它在自己心中唤起的情感，
[00:25.08]concludes that it must be the gateway to a world that lies beyond | 便得出结论说，那一定是一条通道，通往一个超越尘世的世界。
[00:29.91]It is difficult for any of us in moments of intense aesthetic experience | 我们任何人在强烈的审美体验时刻，
[00:35.38]to resist the suggestion that we are catching a glimpse of a light | 都很难抗拒这样的暗示：我们正在瞥见一束光，
[00:39.50]that shines down to us from a different realm of existence, different and, | 它从另一个存在王国照射下来，那王国与我们的不同，而且
[00:45.52]because the experience is intensely moving, in some way higher. | 因为这种体验震撼人心，在某些方面更崇高。
[00:50.94]And, though the gleams blind and dazzle, yet do they convey a hint of beauty and serenity | 而且，尽管这光芒使人目眩眼花，它们确实传递出一丝美与宁静的意味，
[00:57.44]greater than we have known or imagined. Greater too than we can describe; | 比我们所知或所想像的更伟大，也超出了我们所能描述的；
[01:02.99]for language, which was invented to convey the meanings of this world | 因为语言是为了传达这个世界的意义而发明的，
[01:08.00]cannot readily be fitted to the uses of another. | 不能轻易地套用于另一个世界的用途。
[01:12.82]That all great art has this power of suggesting a world beyond is undeniable. | 一切伟大的艺术都具有暗示一个彼岸世界的力量，这一点是无可否认的。
[01:19.84]In some moods, nature shares it. | 在某些心境中，大自然也具有这种力量。
[01:23.37]There is no sky in June so blue that it does not point forward to a bluer, | 六月的天空再蓝，也不会不使人联想到更蓝的天空，
[01:29.09]no sunset so beautiful that it does not waken the vision of a greater beauty, | 没有哪一次日落美得不会唤起一个更美的景象，
[01:34.63]a vision which passes before it is fully glimpsed, | 一个还没有完全看清就已逝去的景象，
[01:38.23]and in passing leaves an indefinable longing and regret. | 它在消逝中留下一种难以名状的渴望和遗憾。
[01:42.48]But, if this world is not merely a bad joke, | 但是，如果这个世界不只是一个拙劣的玩笑，
[01:45.95]life a vulgar flare amid the cool radiance of the stars, | 如果生命不只是璀璨群星寒光之中的一次庸俗的闪光，
[01:50.05]and existence an empty laugh braying across the mysteries; | 如果存在不只是横贯神秘之上的一声空洞的笑声；
[01:54.91]if these intimations of a something behind and beyond | 如果这些背后和彼岸有什么东西的暗示
[01:59.14]are not evil humour born of indigestion, | 不是消化不良产生的恶意，
[02:03.00]or whimsies sent by the devil to mock and madden us, if, in a word | 也不是魔鬼派来嘲弄和折磨我们的怪念头，一句话，如果
[02:08.80]beauty means something yet we must not seek to interpret the meaning. | 美意味着某种东西，那么我们就一定不要去解释这个意义。
[02:14.61]If we glimpse the unutterable, it is unwise to try to utter it, | 如果我们瞥见了不可言传的事物，去妄图言传它是不明智的，
[02:19.73]nor should we seek to invest with significance that which we cannot grasp. | 我们也不应当给我们所不能把握的东西赋予什么意义。
[02:25.93]Beauty in terms of our human meanings is meaningless. | 用我们人类的意义来衡量，美是没有意义的。
